>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. One O atom in the optimized input clearly bonds to S. The other hydrogen-free O is terminal oxo. At these coordinates, S–O⁻, two deprotonated amide N⁻ sites and terminal O²⁻ balance Re(V). The crystalline dioxo form identifies the original species. Localized 5 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths.

