>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Three cyclohexanedione dioxime units form a boron-capped cage. The four-coordinate B carries −1, Each of the three terminal oxime O atoms unbound to B carries −1. The remaining oxime bonds are written as C=N. An external NCS⁻ balances Re(V) together with the cage. B is a single capping atom. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

