>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1039/C4DT01122H","https://doi.org/10.1039/c4dt01122h","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/7031287.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Both benzylic sites are CH. The input skeleton is delocalized. Retain the phenolic ether, the quinonoid C=O at the other end and three Cl⁻, Select the monoanionic ligand and Ti(IV) limiting form; The negative charge drawn at the benzylic site can delocalize through the aromatic ring and amine. The H45 composition of the originally reported compound is recorded separately. Localized 6 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Not equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Not independently verified

