>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. The deposition identifies a neutral chloridooxo Re(V) complex with two monoanionic thiobenzamidinate ligands. Each ligand contains H16 from phenyl H5, two ethyl groups H10 and one N–H. The complete component has H32. The two ligands may use different localized Lewis forms. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The original paper or deposition identifies the ligands, Checked against the supplied coordinates site by site. The atom order and coordinates of all 67 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 64 nonmetal covalent bonds: 62 within range, 1 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 37–41 C-N 1.2796 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

